  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">East Africa Local Hunger Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development Initiatives will produce a policy brief (20 pages) for CAFOD detailing funding to local and national actors (LNAs) in response to hunger crisis and food insecurity in East Africa. This policy brief will specifically focus on funding to South Sudan but include comparative quantitative research for other countries in the region.
This work will provide an understanding of the funding landscape for food crisis response, including how funding reached local and national actors in previous responses, how the current response is unfolding and the perspectives of local partners on the accessibility of funding, the quality of funding (indirect/direct costs, cash flow, financial reporting and disbursements) and the key barriers and enablers to a locally-led response.</narrative>
  </description>
